1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,460
Quentin Tarantino, one of the most acclaimed filmmakers of all time,

2
00:00:03,760 --> 00:00:08,160
known for bringing his bold ideas to life with surreal visuals and mind-bending storytelling.

3
00:00:08,880 --> 00:00:10,460
But he wasn't always a Hollywood icon.

4
00:00:10,900 --> 00:00:13,780
Once he was just an ordinary guy working at a video store.

5
00:00:14,260 --> 00:00:16,940
Until one night, he decided to rewrite his story.

6
00:00:17,320 --> 00:00:18,560
And there was like one night.

7
00:00:18,720 --> 00:00:21,680
Stay up all night long, and rather than give myself excuses,

8
00:00:22,100 --> 00:00:27,060
I would look at everything that I'm up in my life, or everything I'm not doing, or whatever,

9
00:00:27,060 --> 00:00:29,640
and just not give myself any excuses out.

10
00:00:29,640 --> 00:00:31,620
Just like nailing.

11
00:00:31,620 --> 00:00:35,580
And I would spend like all night laying out everything I'm doing that's wrong.

12
00:00:35,820 --> 00:00:38,660
And then I would spend the last two hours figuring out how I can change it.

13
00:00:38,960 --> 00:00:42,480
And as opposed to just doing it and then going to get some sleep.

14
00:00:42,660 --> 00:00:43,700
I decided to change my life.

15
00:00:43,800 --> 00:00:46,040
Today I present you the Tarantino Method.

16
00:00:46,520 --> 00:00:48,580
To follow this process, you'll need three things.

17
00:00:48,740 --> 00:00:50,980
A pen, a notepad, and the dead of night.

18
00:00:51,280 --> 00:00:53,540
When the world is silent and not a soul is awake.

19
00:00:53,900 --> 00:00:55,000
That's when it can happen.

20
00:00:55,440 --> 00:00:55,760
Trust.

21
00:00:55,980 --> 00:00:56,840
Now it begins.

22
00:00:57,040 --> 00:00:58,920
The first page is always going to be the hardest.

23
00:00:58,920 --> 00:01:03,180
But it's really all about getting that ball rolling.

24
00:01:03,180 --> 00:01:08,680
Now that you've started, you have to ask yourself the big, scary, fear-mongering question.

25
00:01:08,680 --> 00:01:19,987
What am I doing wrong Be brutally honest As Quentin himself would say Nail it Take your time Dive deep It gritty It tough But it absolutely necessary

26
00:01:20,587 --> 00:01:21,707
And when you push through,

27
00:01:22,287 --> 00:01:22,607
Boom!

28
00:01:23,167 --> 00:01:24,127
You're halfway there.

29
00:01:26,467 --> 00:01:27,667
It's all out there.

30
00:01:28,047 --> 00:01:28,567
The fears.

31
00:01:28,867 --> 00:01:29,287
The doubts.

32
00:01:29,547 --> 00:01:30,107
The mistakes.

33
00:01:30,387 --> 00:01:30,887
The lessons.

34
00:01:31,127 --> 00:01:31,747
The heartbreak.

35
00:01:31,947 --> 00:01:32,747
All laid out.

36
00:01:33,047 --> 00:01:33,987
Bare for you to see.

37
00:01:34,407 --> 00:01:35,747
Not built up in your mind,

38
00:01:35,927 --> 00:01:36,607
but on paper.

39
00:01:37,067 --> 00:01:37,587
Tangible.

40
00:01:38,927 --> 00:01:45,047
Take a moment because now you have to ask yourself, how can I change it? We're not all

41
00:01:45,047 --> 00:01:49,787
Quentin Tarantino. You might be feeling like you're all written out. So let's make this part

42
00:01:49,787 --> 00:01:55,387
simple. A straightforward list. A hundred ways you can change your life. Quite a simple process.

43
00:01:56,107 --> 00:02:02,047
Take a mistake you've learned and write down a way to change it. Repeat it over and over again

44
00:02:02,047 --> 00:02:08,467
and push forward. Write it down. Adapt. Reflect. Learn and grow. Until finally when you ask

45
00:02:08,467 --> 00:02:10,367
Ask yourself, how can I change my life?

46
00:02:10,367 --> 00:02:12,067
You'll have a hundred ways to do it.

47
00:02:12,067 --> 00:02:15,667
But there's one very important thing you need to remember throughout this whole night.

48
00:02:15,667 --> 00:02:17,167
You gotta actually f***ing do it.
